The issue was due to the way the curved segments were joined to the straight segments. Where there somehow was a 0.025 mm gap. Which is notably bigger than the 1e-5 defined precision in the model. See below, where the circle has radius `10.3` and the points of the line segment are at `Y=-10.2749996185303`.

~~~
#53= IFCDIRECTION((0.,1.));
#54= IFCCARTESIANPOINT((15.,0.));
#55= IFCAXIS2PLACEMENT2D(#54,#53);
#56= IFCCIRCLE(#55,10.3);
#57= IFCTRIMMEDCURVE(#56,(IFCPARAMETERVALUE(0.)),(IFCPARAMETERVALUE(3.14159265358979)),.F.,.PARAMETER.);
#58= IFCCOMPOSITECURVESEGMENT(.CONTINUOUS.,.T.,#57);
#59= IFCCARTESIANPOINT((15.,-10.2749996185303));
#60= IFCCARTESIANPOINT((-15.,-10.2749996185303));
#61= IFCPOLYLINE((#59,#60));
#62= IFCCOMPOSITECURVESEGMENT(.CONTINUOUS.,.T.,#61);
~~~

Before the tolerance was hard limited to the modelling precision which caused the edges to loose the association to one of its vertices, which caused the trouble.

This has been fixed in f71ee35f577dd8658b1f71b48d84db9b92c2a626

